  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Pontoon Crossing",
    "description": "A floating bridge across a harbour, wide enough for the hay wagon. There are no piers and no arches: the deck is laid on logs that float on the water, the way armies and ferrymen have bridged rivers for thousands of years. Because it rides so low, one short ramp on each quay is all it takes to roll a wagon on. 41 bricks.\n\n## How it is built\n\nEach step is a group in the Editor, so you can select it, delete it or build it again yourself.\n\n1. **Harbour**: six blue Slab 4x4s make a stretch of water the road crosses, 12 from quay to quay.\n2. **Floats**: three Logs end to end under each edge of the road, lying on the water.\n3. **Deck**: six wooden Plate 2x4s side by side across the logs, 12 long and 4 wide.\n4. **Rails**: six wooden Fences along each side of the deck.\n5. **Ramps**: four Shallow Slopes on each quay lead from the ground up to the deck. On the east side they are turned 180° (press **R** twice) so they climb toward the bridge.\n6. **Boat**: a sailing boat moored beside the bridge, made from a Plate 2x4 hull turned 90°, a Post for the mast and a Large Window turned 90° for the sail.\n\n## Wide enough for the hay wagon\n\nThe hay wagon is about 2 long and 1.4 wide over its wheels, and it takes up a circle 1.6 across. The ramps are 4 wide, and between the rails the deck is 3.7 wide, which leaves more than 1 to spare on each side. Nothing crosses over the road.\n\nThe top of each ramp is exactly level with the deck, so a wagon rolls on without catching an edge, and the rails are tall enough that it can't drive off into the harbour.\n\n## Bricks\n\n- Harbour: 6 Slab 4x4\n- Floats: 6 Log\n- Deck: 6 Plate 2x4\n- Rails: 12 Fence\n- Ramps: 8 Shallow Slope 2x1\n- Boat: 1 Plate 2x4, 1 Post, 1 Large Window\n\n41 bricks in all.",
